{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/345622-cover-switching","id":345622,"title":"Cover-switching","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-20T03:38:29-08:00","id":345622,"title":"Cover-switching","content":"Alright, so I need an opinion on switching between several different covers. Can a demon &quot;move between&quot; physically separate covers?<br /> <br /> For example, say a Demon is working to maintain Jerry, an office drone. Realizing me needs to check something in his other cover, he excuses himself to the men's room, where, after a turn unobserved, transfers to Maria, a housewife. Since the Demon is a single entity, Jerry is gone (and the coworkers might comment on his long bathroom trip) and Maria is likewise unavailable during Jerry's office hours.<br /> But the important aspect is that Maria does not waltz out of the office men's room.<br /> <br /> This feels like a logical conclusion to draw, but the core book is very sparse on cover-switching; I'm hoping someone who's read the ST guide and/or fiction can weigh in.<br /> <br /> <br /> And a follow-up. If this is the case, what of the unoccupied cover(s)? The book says &quot;they age in stasis,&quot; but there is a big difference from the coworkers stumbling upon a soulless, comatose body in a stall, and a complete disappearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4576-darthdoctor","name":"DarthDoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T04:42:43-08:00","id":345672,"title":"","content":"From how I understand it they just disappear for all others if not active covers.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;move between&quot;: Normally you apepar and disappear on the same location. You can simulate what you want there though with 2 form abilities (the teleportation and the clairvoyance ones) or make a houserule","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T10:21:06-08:00","id":345836,"title":"","content":"Maria is going to have to walk out of the men's room.<br /> <br /> As you said, the demon is a single entity. Cover-switching isn't quite shapeshifting, but it's a bit similar: the demon's previous Cover is replaced by her current Cover, without any movement occurring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T10:36:43-08:00","id":345864,"title":"","content":"(Forgive my poor english)<br /> <br /> Do the clothes of the demon changes when she switch covers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4581-korko","name":"Korko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4581_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T10:40:33-08:00","id":345868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/345622-cover-switching?p=345864#post345864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Forgive my poor english)<br /> <br /> Do the clothes of the demon changes when she switch covers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T10:41:54-08:00","id":345870,"title":"","content":"Yepp they should wouldnt make sense else. For example if you have 1 cover which is an animal and one that is an old man........cover switching would then be quite a disadvantage else if you don't have the same clothes in the new cover as it had when you switched out of that cover last","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T11:46:27-08:00","id":345980,"title":"","content":"All Covers, whether in use or not, are part and parcel of the demon's body, and those not in use can be considered collapsed into a potential state within her. So, yes, in addition to what Rose said, when Maria walks out of the men's room (making it a bad place to change Cover in this situation), if Jerry's coworkers get worried and go into the men's room to check on him, he will be nowhere to be found, no comatose body sitting &quot;in reserve.&quot;<br /> <br /> Can this be inconvenient? Hell yeah. Nobody ever said living multiple lives was easy. The psychic reinforcement of Cover does a little bit of the lifting in making sure people assume you're somewhere reasonable, but if you're keeping up multiple Covers, you have to make sure you can show up in the right places as all of them now and then, or they'll degrade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T11:58:45-08:00","id":345994,"title":"","content":"or that you make a big use out of &quot;alibi&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T12:20:15-08:00","id":346025,"title":"","content":"Well, damn. I was going to have an NPC be revealed to be a Demon, but only after my troupe rescues (what they think is) a prisoner of a Kerberoi, but they've talked to him since the &quot;capture.&quot;<br /> <br /> On second thought, I'll just say that he switched covers and then convinced the Kerberoi that he wasn't the guilty, and walk free.<br /> <br /> It's a little bit of ST fuzz, but my troupe hasn't (IC or OOC) really seen a demon before, but I don't want to grossly disregard the basic precepts of the creature type.<br /> <br /> I suppose as a follow up, what would a Kerberoi think of a Demon? They see beyond the flesh to the souls below (which explains the distaste they have for Prometheans) so they wouldn't think they are human...<br /> <br /> Meh, worst case I'll make up an Embed/Exploit &quot;Trick Kerberoi.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4576-darthdoctor","name":"DarthDoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T12:26:31-08:00","id":346030,"title":"","content":"Especially if the demon is an NPC, it's not at all implausible if he knows some kind of embed/exploit to be in two places at once. In fact, I seem to recall there's one already published, but the NPC's method might be more amenable to being used for the fake-prisoner scheme.<br /> <br /> I would think Kerberoi seem much less likely to care about human/inhuman than living/unliving, and the Unchained are firmly living.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T13:00:42-08:00","id":346044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/345622-cover-switching?p=346030#post346030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially if the demon is an NPC, it's not at all implausible if he knows some kind of embed/exploit to be in two places at once. In fact, I seem to recall there's one already published, but the NPC's method might be more amenable to being used for the fake-prisoner scheme.<br /> <br /> I would think Kerberoi seem much less likely to care about human/inhuman than living/unliving, and the Unchained are firmly living.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is one called Alibi that lets you have your covers at another location than you are yourself. A second one ins in one of the later books which does the same as alibit but for the demonic/true form instead of covers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T15:05:37-08:00","id":346145,"title":"","content":"One of my players has an Interlock called 'Shell and Cup Game' that allows switching to a cover that isn't in the same location. You can't predict where the cover will be, it just appears in a logical place.<br /> <br /> I describe using it as being very similar to switching characters in GTA 5 - you select a cover, and then react to wherever that particular person happens to be at the time. If your cover is Trevor, maybe you discover you're wearing a frilly dress on top of a liqueur store...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T12:55:26-08:00","id":346895,"title":"","content":"Thanks everybody. I'm thinking I'll define an Exploit: Dead Man's Drop. Spend 1 Aether to &quot;step out&quot; of a cover and leave a comatose body behind. After your Prium in days, the cover left behind begins to degrade at a rate of 1 dot per 24 hours left abandoned. While the cover is thus unattended, the demon cannot utilize or benefit from the cover. Separation and merging are both instant actions, with no roll.<br /> <br /> Might be a useful/interesting idea for other ST/players, and I prefer having someone else check that I'm not over-powering my NPCs.<br /> <br /> Drawback: Since the cover is still a part of the Demon, its destructions has ramifications. While the hollow shell left behind has its own health and damage levels (which are added to the current damage when being merged,) its destruction causes feedback to its owner; the Demon suffers its cover rating in aggravated damage, along the lines of the fatality. Eg, visible burns if the body is destroyed by fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4576-darthdoctor","user":"DarthDoctor","date":".  Added a drawback after realizing how potent this Exploit is 12-22-2014, 05:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4576-darthdoctor","name":"DarthDoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T13:56:15-08:00","id":349275,"title":"","content":"That actually sounds like an Interlock between Alibi and Play Possum. No need to make it an Exploit, and I don't think it needs any big drawbacks, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T04:43:27-08:00","id":349768,"title":"","content":"This sounds very interesting, but I can't find Play Possum. Is it in the core?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4576-darthdoctor","name":"DarthDoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T10:25:53-08:00","id":349938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarthDoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/345622-cover-switching?p=349768#post349768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds very interesting, but I can't find Play Possum. Is it in the core?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in Flowers of Hell, the player's guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}